title: Local Government
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/county_hall.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and local_government_timer <= 0
on-arrival: local_government_timer = 5; month_actions += 1

= Local Government

Councils spend a quarter of public money, and many of the biggest are run by Labour. [? if time >= 40 : Ken Livingstone's Greater London Council has cut London Transport fares by a third and flies a red flag over County Hall. ?] Every pound they overspend undoes a pound of the Treasury's cuts.

- @rsg_cut: Cut the Rate Support Grant.
- @rate_capping: Introduce a bill to cap the rates of overspending councils.
- @abolish_rates: Promise to abolish the domestic rates.
- @abolish_glc: Introduce a bill to abolish the GLC and the metropolitan counties.
- @docklands: Create urban development corporations for the docklands.
- @tendering: Make councils put their services out to tender.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@rsg_cut
view-if: rsg_cuts < 3
subtitle: +0.5 budget. The rates go up instead.
on-arrival: rsg_cuts += 1; budget += 0.5; c1_con -= 1; de_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 2; dry_dissent -= 1

The grant from central government is cut again. Councils raise the rates to make up the difference, and the ratepayers blame whoever they voted for last.

@rate_capping
view-if: rate_capping = 0 and rsg_cuts >= 1 and bill_rates = 0 and time >= bill_rates_wait
subtitle: Ratepayers approve. The wets fear for local democracy. Requires a dry Environment Secretary. Law in about seven months.
choose-if: environment_dry = 1 and bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if environment_dry = 0 : [+ environment_secretary +] believes in local democracy. ?][? if environment_dry = 1 : [+ bill_room_text +] ?]
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 3; rebellion += 0.5; bill_new = "rates"
call: bill_introduce

[+ environment_secretary +] publishes the Rates Bill, which will give Whitehall the power to cap the rates of councils that overspend. Ted Heath lets it be known that he will vote against it. Labour councils in Liverpool and Lambeth threaten to defy the law.

@abolish_rates
view-if: rates_pledge = 0
subtitle: Popular now. The Treasury asks what will replace them.
on-arrival: rates_pledge = 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); thatcher_rating += 1; dry_dissent += 2
achievement: rates

You made this promise in 1974, and you meant it. A Green Paper sets out the alternatives: a local sales tax, a local income tax, or a flat charge on every adult. Nobody likes any of them, and the flat charge, which the civil servants call a poll tax, least of all.

@abolish_glc
view-if: glc_abolition = 0 and time >= 50 and bill_glc = 0 and time >= bill_glc_wait
subtitle: The right is delighted. The wets and the Lords will resist. Requires a dry Environment Secretary. Law in about six months.
choose-if: environment_dry = 1 and bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if environment_dry = 0 : [+ environment_secretary +] won't abolish a whole tier of local government. ?][? if environment_dry = 1 : [+ bill_room_text +] ?]
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 4; lib_relation -= 2; rebellion += 0.5; bill_new = "glc"
call: bill_introduce

The government will abolish the Greater London Council and the six metropolitan county councils. Ken Livingstone hangs the London unemployment figures from the roof of County Hall, across the river from Parliament, and starts a campaign to save it.

@docklands
view-if: docklands = 0
subtitle: -0.5 budget. New jobs, and a showcase for enterprise.
on-arrival: docklands = 1; budget -= 0.5; economic_growth += 0.2; unemployment -= 0.1; ru_london -= 0.4; ru_northwest -= 0.2; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 2
achievement: docklands

The Environment Secretary creates development corporations for the London and Merseyside docklands, and Sir Geoffrey Howe declares the first enterprise zones, free of rates and planning controls. Eight square miles of derelict wharves on the Isle of Dogs wait for the developers.

@tendering
view-if: council_tendering = 0
subtitle: +0.5 budget. The council unions lose ground.
on-arrival: council_tendering = 1; budget += 0.5; union_power -= 2; dry_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 1

Council building and maintenance departments must now win their work in competition with private firms. In some towns the direct labour organisation wins; in many it doesn't.
